steps.text:
`if` runs a block of code only when a condition is true. `else` runs when it's false.

```c
if (hp > 0) {
    printf("alive\n");
} else {
    printf("dead\n");
}
```

Comparison operators: `==` equal, `!=` not equal, `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`.

Careful: `=` assigns and `==` compares. `if (x = 5)` is a classic bug.

