steps.text:
A `while` loop repeats its block as long as the condition stays true.

```c
int i = 1;
while (i <= 3) {
    printf("%d\n", i);
    i++;
}
```

This prints 1, 2, 3. Forget the `i++` and the loop runs forever. On this site, an infinite loop gets stopped after 3 seconds.

