steps.solution:
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    int sum = 0;
    int x;
    while (scanf("%d", &x) == 1) {
        // stop at 0, skip negatives, add the rest
        if (x == 0) break;
        if (x < 0) continue;
        sum += x;
    }
    printf("%d\n", sum);
    return 0;
}

steps.text:
A `do { } while (cond);` loop checks its condition at the **end**, so the body always runs at least once. It's perfect for "ask until valid" input and for menus.

```c
int x;
do {
    scanf("%d", &x);
} while (x < 1 || x > 5);
```

Note the semicolon after `while (...)`.

