steps.text:
A loop inside a loop runs the inner loop completely for every round of the outer one. That's how you walk a grid.

```c
for (int row = 0; row < 2; row++) {
    for (int col = 0; col < 3; col++) {
        printf("*");
    }
    printf("\n");
}
```
prints two rows of three stars.

