C++ grew out of C, so almost all your C knowledge carries over. The first visible difference is output. Instead of `printf`, C++ uses **streams**:

```cpp
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::cout << "Kills: " << 25 << "\n";
}
```

- `std::cout` is the standard output stream.
- `<<` sends things into it, left to right. No format specifiers needed: it knows the types.
- `std::` means these names live in the **standard namespace**.
